{"id":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000003:1","agent":"claude-code","sessionId":"00000000-0000-4000-8000-000000000001","projectPath":"c:\\Users\\dev\\Downloads\\hackNCanalysis","ts":"2026-10-11T04:03:45.218Z","seq":2,"kind":"prompt","text":"Act as a senior backend software engineer. Build a Python module using `asyncio` that takes a short-form video transcript, finds candidate full-length YouTube videos, evaluates their text similarity, and returns the best matching video URL.\n\nWorkflow & Requirements:\n\n1. Metadata Extraction (Speaker & Anchor Quote):\n   - Use an LLM call (e.g., Groq `llama-3.3-70b-versatile` or Claude `claude-3-5-haiku`) to parse the short transcript.\n   - Extract:\n     a) `speaker_and_event`: Name of speaker(s) + event type (e.g., \"Donald Trump Kamala Harris debate 2024\").\n     b) `unique_phrase`: A verbatim, highly distinct 6-8 word phrase from the transcript.\n   - Construct a targeted search query string: `\"{speaker_and_event}\" \"{unique_phrase}\"`\n\n2. Search YouTube Candidates:\n   - Search YouTube for candidate videos using the official YouTube Data API v3 (`google-api-python-client`) or `yt-dlp` search mode.\n   - Fetch metadata for the top 3-5 candidate video IDs (Title, Video ID, URL, Duration). Filter out any short videos under 3 minutes long.\n\n3. Fast Fuzzy Comparison & Early Exit:\n   - For each candidate video ID:\n     a) Fetch its full transcript text using `youtube-transcript-api`.\n     b) Normalize both texts (lower-case, remove punctuation and extra whitespace).\n     c) Use `rapidfuzz.fuzz.partial_ratio` to check if the short transcript exists inside the long candidate text.\n     d) If the match score is >= 75%:\n        - Stop checking further candidates immediately (early exit).\n        - Return this video URL as the match.\n\n4. Output Format:\n   Return a dictionary:\n   {\n     \"status\": \"success\" | \"not_found\",\n     \"match_score\": float,            # e.g., 88.5\n     \"video_id\": str,                 # YouTube video ID\n     \"video_url\": str,                # Clean YouTube video URL\n     \"title\": str                     # Full video title\n   }\n\n5. Exception Handling:\n   - Handle missing captions gracefully on individual candidate videos (skip to th…[truncated 330 chars]","meta":{"sources":["pasted"]}}
